{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Motivation\n\nEvery demo recording spends ~50–200 GraphQL points and breaks outright while the quota is exhausted (three re-records on 2026-09-07). The GitHub and Projects demos depend on the live API, so the GIFs are neither cheap nor reproducible.\n\n## Spec\n\n- A recording-only, **undocumented** environment variable `VIG_GH_FIXTURE=<dir>` (same standing as `VIG_PROCS_ROOT_PID`): when set, vig never runs `gh` and instead reads the JSON responses (issues, PRs, runs, projects, views, item / field lists) from `<dir>`.\n- `tape/fixtures/` holds the demo project (View 1 / By status / Timeline, with dates and a filter) and the GitHub page responses; the `demo-github-*` and `demo-projects` tapes use them. GIFs become deterministic and `mise run demo:all` needs zero API calls.\n- Fixtures are the verbatim `gh … --format json` outputs, with a refresh task (`mise run fixtures:refresh` — the only step that touches the API).\n- The same fixtures drive integration tests: page initialisation through rendering, verified with ratatui's `TestBackend`.","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-08T08:11:49Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":170,"state":"CLOSED","title":"Record demos and run integration tests from API-free fixtures"}
